  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0pt;mso-ascii-font-family:Aptos;\r\nmso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-hansi-font-family:Aptos;mso-hansi-theme-font:\r\nminor-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;\r\nmso-fareast-language:EN-US&quot;&gt;The proposed part single storey and part two storey\r\nrear extensions, by reason of their cumulative scale, bulk, massing and design,\r\nparticularly the flat roof first floor rear extension in combination with the\r\nground floor rear addition, would result in an overly dominant and\r\ninsufficiently subordinate form of development, which would not complement the\r\nexisting roof form and would appear as a contrived roof form that detracts from\r\nthe character and appearance of the existing dwelling. The proposal would fail\r\nto respect the original form, proportions and architectural character of the\r\nhost dwelling, resulting in an incongruous addition that would cause harm to\r\nthe character and appearance of the property and the terrace of which it forms\r\npart. The development would therefore be contrary to Chapters 12 and 14 of the\r\nNational Planning Policy Framework (2026), Policies D3 and D4 of the London\r\nPlan (2021), and Policies D12.1, D12.2, D12.3 and D12.4 of the Merton Local\r\nPlan (2024).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
